BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tokyo-biennale-2027-social-dive@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tokyo Biennale 2027: SOCIAL DIVE open call for artists an
 d curators
DESCRIPTION:SOCIAL DIVE is Tokyo Biennale's open call\, now in its third ed
 ition and\, for 2027\, open to both international and domestic applicants 
 (the 2019 round drew roughly 1\,500 overseas applications and the 2025 int
 ernational-only round roughly 1\,400). Artists and curators propose projec
 ts to be presented as part of Tokyo Biennale 2027\, whose theme is 'From M
 e to Us'. THEME: general producer Masato Nakamura frames the biennale agai
 nst an age of conflict and division\, arguing that to avoid repeating memo
 ries of war\, violence and exclusion we must reexamine the wisdom and cult
 ural resources passed down across generations. Tokyo carries the memories 
 of neighbourhoods dating back to the Edo period\, twice suffered great los
 s through the Great Kanto Earthquake and the Second World War\, and each t
 ime was rebuilt through the strength of its citizens\; it is also an inter
 national city where different languages\, memories\, beliefs\, wounds and 
 hopes intersect. Quoting Kenzaburo Oe\, 'I cannot live my life over again.
  But we can live our lives over again'\, the call proposes that when a sin
 gle 'me' encounters others and reconnects relationships\, a new consciousn
 ess of 'us' emerges. Art projects are treated as a form of cultural prescr
 iption\, reconnecting people with people\, people with places and people w
 ith memories. ELIGIBILITY: open to artists\, curators\, researchers\, coll
 ectives and practitioners in related fields active in Japan and abroad\; a
 pplicants must be 18 or older at the time of application\; there are no re
 strictions on nationality\, place of residence or base of operations\; par
 ticipants must be able to work in Tokyo during the designated period. ACCE
 PTED FORMATS: artwork creation\, exhibitions\, performances\, video works\
 , tours\, workshops\, participatory projects\, research projects and curat
 orial projects. Applications cover both artwork production by artists and 
 art project proposals by curators. APPLY via the Google Form linked from s
 ocialdive.jp/en (a Google account is required) during the application peri
 od 17 July to 30 September 2026\, 23:59 JST. Read the official call docume
 ntation for full eligibility requirements and guidelines.\n\nOrganisation:
  Tokyo Biennale\nLocation: Tokyo\, Japan. Selected participants carry out 
 residency-based production\, research\, meetings\, preparation and impleme
 ntation in Tokyo during a designated period. No restrictions on nationalit
 y\, place of residence or base of operations.\nAward: Travel up to JPY 300
 \,000 (economy class\, one person maximum)\, accommodation in Tokyo\, a pr
 oject development budget of up to JPY 200\,000\, and a JPY 100\,000 honora
 rium. Additional support includes venue coordination\, interpretation\, tr
 anslation and an invitation letter. No application fee.\nDuration: Residen
 cy-based work in Tokyo during a designated period\, with the project prese
 nted as part of Tokyo Biennale 2027.\n\nMore: https://socialdive.jp/en/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://socialdive.jp/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Tokyo\, Japan. Selected participants carry out residency-based pro
 duction\, research\, meetings\, preparation and implementation in Tokyo du
 ring a designated period. No restrictions on nationality\, place of reside
 nce or base of operations.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ars-biologica-artxscience-residency-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ars Biologica ArtXScience Residency 2027-2028 (Ars Electr
 onica x Ceske Budejovice ECoC 2028)
DESCRIPTION:A fully funded art-science residency from Ars Electronica and C
 eske Budejovice\, European Capital of Culture 2028\, exploring how art and
  science can collaborate on urgent environmental challenges: climate emerg
 ence\, sustainable agriculture\, geoengineering\, permaculture\, water res
 ource management\, and the broader ecological impacts on local communities
 . Selected residents work in direct collaboration with local scientists in
  Ceske Budejovice. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, designers\, creatives and arti
 st collectives with more than 5 years of professional creative practice an
 d documented interdisciplinary work\; experience in community engagement a
 nd science collaborations is essential\; applicants must be 18+\, of any n
 ationality\, and legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. WHAT YOU G
 ET: a EUR 24\,000 package (EUR 6\,000 artist fee\, up to EUR 15\,000 produ
 ction\, up to EUR 3\,000 travel and subsistence) plus one month of housing
  covered separately\; two winners are selected. STRUCTURE: the residency r
 uns January 2027 to April 2028\, with a required on-site stay of up to one
  month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/September 2027\
 , and a March 2028 stay for festival installation\, exhibition and deinsta
 llation. HOW TO APPLY: online form with project title\, a written proposal
  of max 250 words\, a scientific direction statement (max 100 words)\, art
 istic vision (max 100 words)\, community connection plan (max 100 words)\,
  a super short pitch (3 to 30 words)\, 3 to 7 images\, an optional 1-minut
 e video\, a portfolio link and contact information. Two-round selection (o
 nline application then interview)\; winners notified by November 2026. Dea
 dline 28 September 2026 at midnight CET.\n\nOrganisation: Ars Electronica 
 and Ceske Budejovice - European Capital of Culture 2028\nLocation: Ceske B
 udejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any nationality aged 18+
  who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Required on-site s
 tays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/
 September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibition and deinstal
 lation.\nAward: EUR 24\,000 total package per winner: EUR 6\,000 artist fe
 e\, up to EUR 15\,000 production budget\, and up to EUR 3\,000 for travel\
 , accommodation and subsistence\, plus a separate budget covering one mont
 h of housing in Ceske Budejovice. Two positions available. Free to apply.\
 nDuration: January 2027 to April 2028\, with on-site blocks in early 2027 
 and March 2028\n\nMore: https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars
 -biologica-art-science-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars-biologica-art-scienc
 e-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ceske Budejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any natio
 nality aged 18+ who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Req
 uired on-site stays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional 
 stay in August/September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibiti
 on and deinstallation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:studio-alta-residence-2027-open-calls@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Studio ALTA Residence 2027: four residency open calls (Pr
 ague)
DESCRIPTION:Prague performance venue Studio ALTA announces four residency o
 pen calls for 2027\, all with a single deadline of 10 September 2026. RESE
 ARCH HOUSE (19 to 28 April 2027): a shared residential laboratory for thre
 e art projects or individual artists in the early stages of exploration an
 d experimentation\, or reopening an existing finished work (performance\, 
 installation\, object\, video) to transform it into another form such as a
  workshop\, text or performance-lecture. Includes a 10-day residency\, a f
 ee of CZK 12\,000 per project\, shared studio\, individual workspace and f
 acilitated exchange meetings\; the research output must be shared publicly
  as a work-in-progress in a form based on participants' needs. REST HOUSE 
 (March to November 2027): a five-day residential spa for overloaded collea
 gues from the arts sector\, with no required output or activities\; restri
 cted to people working in production\, dramaturgy\, curation\, PR\, techni
 cal and other supporting artistic professions in the Czech independent sec
 tor. Two guests are chosen by lottery (fee CZK 6\,000 per person)\; the pu
 blic draw is announced 16 September 2026. HOUSE IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD (9 to 
 18 August 2027): for one performative art project created with the local c
 ommunity and designed or adapted for public space in Liben and its surroun
 dings\; this year's call focuses on the 55+ target group. Includes a fee o
 f CZK 30\,000 per project\, rehearsal and indoor facilities (primarily out
 door spaces)\, dramaturgic\, production\, technical and PR consultation\, 
 connections to partner organisations\, and 7 days of intensive production 
 and technical support in the final phase. A public premiere or work-in-pro
 gress in public space at the end of the residency is required. HOUSE OF SW
 EAT (1 to 10 February 2027): for one performative art project designed or 
 adapted for the specific environment of the Studio ALTA sauna and its imme
 diate surroundings\, seeking new ways of working with intimate space\, pro
 ximity to the audience and non-traditional formats. Includes a fee of CZK 
 15\,000 per project\, a 10-day residency\, sauna and rehearsal spaces\, dr
 amaturgic\, production\, technical and PR consultation\, and 2 days of int
 ensive final-phase support\; a public work-in-progress or premiere in the 
 sauna within the 9 to 12 February 2027 programme block is required. Projec
 ts at any stage of development can apply to the production calls\, and sel
 ected projects may be included in Studio ALTA's year-round programme. TIME
 LINE: deadline 10 September 2026\; results 3 weeks after the deadline (30 
 September 2026)\; a Q&A Zoom call takes place 10 August 2026 at 3:00 PM. A
 pply via the registration forms on the call page.\n\nOrganisation: Studio 
 ALTA\nLocation: Studio ALTA\, Prague (Liben district)\, Czech Republic. Th
 ree of the four calls are open internationally\; the Rest House call is re
 served for supporting-profession arts workers active in the Czech independ
 ent sector.\nAward: Residency fees paid to participants: Research House CZ
 K 12\,000 per project\; Rest House CZK 6\,000 per person\; House in the Ne
 ighborhood CZK 30\,000 per project\; House of Sweat CZK 15\,000 per projec
 t. All include workspace at Studio ALTA\; the two production residencies a
 dd dramaturgic\, production\, technical and PR support. Free to apply.\nDu
 ration: Programme dependent: 5 to 10 days\, at various points between Febr
 uary and November 2027\n\nMore: https://www.altart.cz/rezidence-2027/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.altart.cz/rezidence-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Studio ALTA\, Prague (Liben district)\, Czech Republic. Three of t
 he four calls are open internationally\; the Rest House call is reserved f
 or supporting-profession arts workers active in the Czech independent sect
 or.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:surface-design-association-air-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260815
SUMMARY:Deadline: Surface Design Association: Artist in Residence 2026-27 (
 virtual)
DESCRIPTION:The Surface Design Association's Artist in Residence programme 
 is built to develop skills\, open up relationships and support fiber and t
 extile artists through a studio project that pushes their practice. The re
 sidency is entirely virtual and runs across a full year\, which is the poi
 nt: it removes the travel\, housing and time-away barriers that keep many 
 practitioners out of in-person residencies. One artist is selected annuall
 y by a panel of SDA staff\, board members and committee volunteers. WHAT I
 T INVOLVES: studio visits across the year\, social media programming\, and
  meetings with the SDA community\, plus further programming shaped around 
 the resident's own skills and interests\, which can include teaching onlin
 e workshops\, contributing to SDA publications\, jurying exhibitions or jo
 ining panels. FUNDING: a $2\,000 studio stipend for the project\, plus up 
 to $2\,000 in additional compensation for programming work\, targeting abo
 ut $4\,000 total. ELIGIBILITY: emerging\, mid-career and established artis
 ts\; US-based and international applicants welcome\; students and professi
 onals may apply\; applicants must hold current SDA membership (from $85 pe
 r year\, $60 for students). APPLICATION: a portfolio of 10 images with ful
 l artwork information (title\, year\, materials\, technique\, dimensions\,
  photo credit)\, a detailed CV\, essay responses on artistic goals\, progr
 amming interests and professional development\, and demographic informatio
 n. No application fee. The 2026-27 cycle closes 14 August 2026.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Surface Design Association (SDA)\nLocation: Fully virtual. Open to 
 US-based and international applicants\; current SDA membership is required
 .\nAward: $2\,000 studio stipend\, plus up to $2\,000 further compensation
  for programming work (SDA aims for roughly $4\,000 in total per resident)
 . No application fee\, but applicants must be current SDA members (members
 hip from $85 per year\, $60 for students).\nDuration: One year\, virtual\,
  October 2026 to August 2027\n\nMore: https://www.surfacedesign.org/air_fo
 rm/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.surfacedesign.org/air_form/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Fully virtual. Open to US-based and international applicants\; cur
 rent SDA membership is required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:instituto-sacatar-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: Instituto Sacatar: Sacatar Fellowship 2027 (Bahia\, Brazi
 l)
DESCRIPTION:Brazil's longest-running artist residency\, on the island of It
 aparica across the bay from Salvador\, hosting six to eight artists per se
 ssion for roughly eight weeks. Open to all creative disciplines and\, unus
 ually for this region\, to all nationalities\, which makes it one of the f
 ew genuinely international residencies in Latin America. Sacatar provides 
 full hosting (private room\, three meals daily\, individual studio\, laund
 ry\, local logistics and connections) but explicitly does NOT provide a st
 ipend\, airfare to Salvador\, art materials or discretionary local expense
 s\, so applicants must fund their own travel. Individual artists only\; gr
 oup proposals are not accepted and former Sacatar Fellows may not reapply.
  COVID vaccination is required. NOTE: there is a USD 25 application fee. A
 pply through SlideRoom by 28 August 2026. Contact info@sacatar.org.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Instituto Sacatar\nLocation: Itaparica island\, Bahia\, Brazil.
  Open to all nationalities.\nAward: Fully hosted residency: private bedroo
 m with attached bathroom\, three meals a day (except Saturday evenings\, S
 undays and Brazilian holidays)\, an individual studio suited to the discip
 line\, weekly laundry\, logistical support and airport transfer from Salva
 dor. NO STIPEND\, no airfare and no materials budget. USD 25 application f
 ee. One French artist may additionally receive airfare and a stipend throu
 gh Villa Fatumbi.\nDuration: Approximately eight weeks\; specific session 
 dates are listed in the application.\n\nMore: https://sacatar.org/en/fello
 wships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sacatar.org/en/fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Itaparica island\, Bahia\, Brazil. Open to all nationalities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:new-emergence-art-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: New Emergence Art Prize 2026
DESCRIPTION:The New Emergence Art Prize 2026 is an international open call 
 for emerging artists\, presented by New Emergence Art. There is no set the
 me and work may be submitted in any medium. AWARDS: a prize fund worth ove
 r GBP 5\,000 across nine awards supporting artists through cash prizes\, a
 rtist materials\, mentoring\, and a residency\, including a GBP 1\,000 Gra
 nd Prize\, a two-week NG Art Creative Residency in Provence\, France (wort
 h EUR 2\,000)\, a GBP 300 Founder's Prize cash award\, and materials or su
 bscription awards from Staedtler UK\, Rosemary & Co\, GreatArt\, Michael H
 arding\, and The Art Ladder. ELIGIBILITY: open internationally to emerging
  artists\; entrants may submit up to three original artworks that represen
 t the quality\, originality and direction of their practice. Final selecti
 ons are made by an independent judging panel considering concept\, executi
 on\, originality and impact. Shortlisted artists are featured in an online
  exhibition running 11 August to 7 September 2026. NOTE: there is a paid e
 ntry fee (amount set at the entry step). DEADLINE: 3 August 2026\, 23:59 B
 ST. Apply via https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply.\n\nOrganisation: New 
 Emergence Art\nLocation: International\; open worldwide. Shortlist shown i
 n an online exhibition.\nAward: Prize fund worth over GBP 5\,000 across ni
 ne awards\, including a GBP 1\,000 Grand Prize cash award\, a two-week NG 
 Art Creative Residency in Provence\, France (worth EUR 2\,000)\, a GBP 300
  Founder's Prize cash award\, and materials or subscription awards from St
 aedtler UK\, Rosemary & Co\, GreatArt\, Michael Harding\, and The Art Ladd
 er. NOTE: there is a paid entry fee.\nDuration: One-off prize\; shortliste
 d artists shown in an online exhibition 11 August to 7 September 2026\n\nM
 ore: https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International\; open worldwide. Shortlist shown in an online exhib
 ition.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ted-posca-global-artist-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: TED & POSCA Global Artist Residency 2026: Visible Mending
DESCRIPTION:TED (the global platform for ideas and storytelling) and POSCA 
 (a creative brand by uni Brands Corporation) are launching a new kind of a
 rtist residency: a globally distributed cohort of artists working across d
 ifferent geographies\, cultures\, and communities\, united by a shared dri
 ve to shape public life through art. Fine Acts\, the external curatorial p
 artner selected by TED & POSCA\, leads the curation\, creative direction\,
  and coordination. There is no single location and no central studio: sele
 cted artists work within their own communities\, following a shared creati
 ve constraint (a unifying conceptual framework around repair\, hope\, and 
 beauty)\, with projects unfolding in public space\, community participatio
 n as a key part of the work\, and process mattering as much as outcome. 20
 26 THEME\, VISIBLE MENDING: inspired in part by Kintsugi (the Japanese pra
 ctice of repairing broken ceramics with gold)\, the theme explores repair 
 as a creative and civic act\, inviting artists to consider how wounds\, ru
 ptures\, and imperfections can become sites of transformation\, and to mak
 e processes of repair visible through public interventions that spark refl
 ection\, dialogue\, and collective imagination. In 2026\, four artists wil
 l be selected to develop community-rooted public interventions to be imple
 mented in 2027. AWARD: each selected artist receives a total of USD 15\,00
 0 to cover artist fees\, production costs/community activation\, and docum
 entation\, plus a production budget and tools from POSCA\, creative direct
 ion and storytelling support\, and visibility through TED and Fine Acts' g
 lobal platforms. While the residency term is one year\, the initiative wil
 l run for multiple years (2027\, 2028\, 2029)\, expanding the cohort year 
 by year and building an evolving global archive of civic artistic interven
 tions. Apply by 31 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: TED & POSCA (curated by Fin
 e Acts)\nLocation: Globally distributed\; no single location or central st
 udio. Selected artists work within their own communities\, with projects u
 nfolding in public space.\nAward: Each selected artist receives a total of
  USD 15\,000 (covering artist fees\, production costs/community activation
 \, and documentation)\, plus a production budget and tools from POSCA\, cr
 eative direction and storytelling support\, and visibility through TED and
  Fine Acts' global platforms.\nDuration: One-year residency term\; communi
 ty-rooted public interventions developed in 2026 for implementation in 202
 7. The initiative runs for multiple years (2027\, 2028\, 2029)\, expanding
  the cohort year by year.\n\nMore: https://fineacts.co/ted-posca-residency
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fineacts.co/ted-posca-residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Globally distributed\; no single location or central studio. Selec
 ted artists work within their own communities\, with projects unfolding in
  public space.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:casa-pip-residency-filmmakers-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: CASA PIP Residency for Filmmakers
DESCRIPTION:CASA PIP is a residency program in Portugal founded and run by 
 filmmakers. It encourages residents to slow down and play\, providing film
 makers with the time\, peace\, space\, and general "rulelessness" to move 
 meaningfully forward on their work\, whether it is a whole project or just
  the budding idea for one. The residency is free to attend. ELIGIBILITY: o
 pen internationally to filmmakers. There is a EUR 35 application fee. Dead
 line: July 31\, 2026.\n\nOrganisation: CASA PIP\nLocation: Portugal\; open
  internationally to filmmakers.\nAward: Free residency (no cost to attend)
 \, offering time\, space\, and peace to work on a project or an early idea
 . A EUR 35 application fee applies.\nDuration: Residency\n\nMore: https://
 casapip.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://casapip.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Portugal\; open internationally to filmmakers.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oif-artist-mobility-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: OIF: Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultu
 ral Goods 2026 (Francophonie)
DESCRIPTION:The OIF Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultural
  Goods programme provides grants of up to EUR 5\,000 for mobility (travel\
 , accommodation\, visa fees\, logistics) and up to EUR 2\,500 for circulat
 ion of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs) within the Fran
 cophone zone\; both can be combined. ELIGIBILITY: professional artists and
  established artistic collectives with a demonstrated connection to the Fr
 ancophone space (by nationality\, working language\, or artistic collabora
 tions)\, residing in an OIF member state\, with minimum 2 years of experie
 nce in the cultural or artistic sector\; must directly manage the project 
 (not act as intermediaries)\; one application per individual per call. ELI
 GIBLE DISCIPLINES: live performance (music\, theatre\, dance\, comedy\, st
 orytelling)\, cinema/audiovisual\, literature/publishing\, and visual arts
 . PRIORITY given to projects promoting gender equality\, women artists\, c
 reators under 35\, and South-South mobility. Projects must take place betw
 een 25 March and 30 November 2026. Multiple selection sessions throughout 
 the year\; call open until 31 August 2026. Information webinars: 11 March\
 , 13 May\, and 8 July 2026 at 3 PM Paris time. Contact: culture.dlc@franco
 phonie.org. Apply at https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicatio
 ns/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Organisation internationale de la Francophonie (OIF)\nLocation: Fra
 ncophone zone (OIF member states globally)\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 for ar
 tist mobility (travel\, accommodation\, visas\, logistics). Up to EUR 2\,5
 00 for circulation of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs).
  Both can be combined. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies or tours
  of 5 days to 3 months. Projects must take place between 25 March and 30 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nMore: https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicat
 ions/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applications/soutien-a-la-ci
 rculation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Francophone zone (OIF member states globally)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lee-ufan-arles-art-environment-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Lee Ufan Arles: Prix Art & Environnement 2026 (Residency 
 + Exhibition Prize)
DESCRIPTION:The Prix Art & Environnement (4th edition)\, awarded by Lee Ufa
 n Arles and Maison Guerlain\, supports an artist working at the intersecti
 on of art and the natural environment. The prize winner receives a funded 
 6–8 week production residency in Arles in early 2027\, including product
 ion space\, accommodation\, and mentorship from Lee Ufan Arles staff\, cul
 minating in a solo summer 2027 exhibition. ELIGIBILITY: open to all artist
 s of any discipline and nationality\, with no age or degree requirements\;
  candidates must demonstrate at least one solo exhibition and one or more 
 group exhibitions. DEADLINE: 31 July 2026. APPLY via the Google Form linke
 d from the Lee Ufan Arles website.\n\nOrganisation: Lee Ufan Arles and Mai
 son Guerlain\nLocation: Arles\, France (residency and exhibition)\nAward: 
 Funded residency (production space + accommodation) in Arles. No cash priz
 e amount specified. No application fee.\nDuration: 6–8 weeks residency i
 n early 2027\, followed by a solo summer 2027 exhibition\n\nMore: https://
 en.leeufan-arles.org/evenements/art-environment-prize?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://en.leeufan-arles.org/evenements/art-environment-prize?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Arles\, France (residency and exhibition)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:revitalizing-rituals-2026-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260720
SUMMARY:Deadline: Revitalizing Rituals 2026 Open Call
DESCRIPTION:Revitalizing Rituals invites artists from all disciplines -- so
 und\, movement\, visual arts\, installation\, performance\, and transdisci
 plinary practices -- to join a research-creation journey across two landsc
 apes: Bhar Lazreg in Tunisia and the wetlands of Somogy County in Hungary.
  The project explores rituals as living forms of belonging: reconnecting c
 ommunities\, land\, memory\, food\, ecological reciprocity\, and the more-
 than-human world. Selected artists work with local communities as co-parti
 cipants in a shared inquiry into moving from extraction toward reciprocity
 . Organised by Homo Faber Alapítvány (Hungary). AMOUNT: EUR 6\,000 gross
  artist fee and production budget\; international travel and per diems cov
 ered\; on-site accommodation provided. ELIGIBILITY: minimum 5 years of act
 ive artistic practice\; portfolio reflecting interest in situated or relat
 ional work\; no formal degree required\; working language is English (loca
 l language navigation valued)\; must be available for the full residency c
 ycle including all international travel\; must be able to legally receive 
 the fee and invoice the organising partners from country of residence. Str
 ongly encourages applications from historically marginalised or underrepre
 sented voices. KEY DATES: Application Deadline 19 July 2026 (midnight) -- 
 note the open call PDF also references a 5 July date\; the officially prom
 oted deadline is 19 July\; Online Q&A 29 June 2026\, 14:00 Tunisia / 15:00
  CET (register at https://forms.gle/brnZvXvFe4JB8zL26)\; Online Conversati
 ons with shortlisted artists: mid July to mid August 2026\; Selection Resu
 lts: 31 August 2026\; Placemaking Camp: 1 week\, end of November 2026\, Hu
 ngary\; Storytellers Camp: 1 week\, March 2027\, Tunisia\; Residency Perio
 d: minimum 1 month (splittable)\, April to July 2027\; Final Presentation:
  August 2027\; Closing Event: 3 days\, winter/early spring 2028\, Hungary.
  Apply via the open call form linked at https://homofaber.hu/wp-content/up
 loads/2026/06/Artist-Open-Call-FINAL-in-the-RR-form.pdf.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Homo Faber Alapítvány (Homo Faber Foundation)\nLocation: Bhar Lazreg\, T
 unisia and Somogy County\, Hungary\; multi-stage in-person residency acros
 s both sites.\nAward: EUR 6\,000 gross artist fee and production budget\; 
 international travel and per diems covered\; on-site accommodation provide
 d. No application fee.\nDuration: Multi-stage residency: Placemaking Camp 
 (1 week\, November 2026\, Hungary)\; Storytellers Camp (1 week\, March 202
 7\, Tunisia)\; Residency Period (minimum 1 month\, April-July 2027)\; publ
 ic presentation (August 2027)\; Closing Event (3 days\, winter/early sprin
 g 2028\, Hungary).\n\nMore: https://homofaber.hu/wp-content/uploads/2026/0
 6/Artist-Open-Call-FINAL-in-the-RR-form.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://homofaber.hu/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Artist-Open-Call-FINAL-
 in-the-RR-form.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Bhar Lazreg\, Tunisia and Somogy County\, Hungary\; multi-stage in
 -person residency across both sites.
END:VEVENT
